          "text": "<p>A drunk calculator or alcohol intoxication calculator estimates your blood alcohol percentage calculator metric to give you a clinical representation of your impairment. At 0.02% to 0.04% BAC, you may feel mild relaxation. By 0.05% to 0.07%, minor impairment in balance, speech, and coordination begins. At 0.08% BAC (the legal limit in many areas) and above, cognitive function and motor skills are significantly degraded. While a how drunk am i calculator can estimate your impairment based on standard averages, physical reactions vary widely based on tolerance, genetics, and food intake.</p>"
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How long after drinking does it take for my BAC to drop? (e.g. BAC after 2 hours)",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "<p>Your BAC continues to change depending on the timeline of your drinks. For example, if you check your BAC after 2 hours of having 1 or 2 beers, your body will have already metabolized a portion of the alcohol (approx. 0.03% total reduction). However, if you drink rapidly (e.g. an alcohol level after 3 beers in under an hour), your peak BAC will occur around 45 minutes after your last drink, and then decrease slowly over the following hours. A when can i drive calculator helps trace this curve to estimate when your BAC will fall below the legal threshold.</p>"
        }
      }
    ]
  }
  </script>

